router B:
  1. POST /system/backup/save {"name":"bk"}
       pre-apply backup of router b
  2. DELETE /user/*3
       remove bob (not on router a)
  3. PATCH /ip/service/*3 {"port":"22"}
       update ssh to match router a
skipped:
  user alice [A→B]: user passwords are not readable over REST; creating this user would leave it with no password
  user admin [B→A]: changes group of the user mtha logs in to router a as; that could lock mtha out
  user api-b [A→B]: mtha logs in to router b as this user; removing it would lock mtha out
  ip/service www-ssl [A→B]: changes port of router b's REST API service; mtha could lose its connection mid-apply
  ip/service api [A→B]: entries in this section are built in; they can be changed but not added
